allets today. Concrete pour scheduled for Friday morning. Bennett plans to work every Saturday. I didn't receive Bennett time card from Hayden today.","subs":[],"survey":[{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""}],"sig":"raken/sig/2025-01-15.png","sigTs":1736995140000,"source":"Raken PDF"},{"id":"raken-bluesky-2025-01-16","pid":"raken-bluesky","date":"2025-01-16","by":"Jeff Pool","site":[{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-16-00.jpg","ts":1736994900000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-16-01.jpg","ts":1737086940000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-16-02.jpg","ts":1737087000000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-16-03.jpg","ts":1737087000000,"cap":""}],"att":[{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-16-04.jpg","ts":1737087000000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-16-05.jpg","ts":1737087000000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-16-06.jpg","ts":1737087000000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-16-07.jpg","ts":1737087000000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-16-08.jpg","ts":1737087000000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-16-09.jpg","ts":1737087000000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-16-10.jpg","ts":1737087000000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-16-11.jpg","ts":1737087000000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-16-12.jpg","ts":1737087000000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-16-13.jpg","ts":1737087000000,"cap":""}],"wx":[{"t":30,"c":"Clear","w":"10","p":".0","h":"79"},{"t":44,"c":"Clear","w":"0","p":".0","h":"53"},{"t":49,"c":"Clear","w":"8","p":".0","h":"48"}],"notes":"I spoke with Russel regarding the Bennett time card yesterday and asked him to please revise it to hours and equipment that re\ufb02ects the actual time worked. He said no he will not revise it. Do to not have the correct parts and having to reorder due to missing information he bid on. Went on to say all men and equipment worked just not at the same time during the day. I expressed to Russel we can't have anyone at anytime standing around waiting, as I pointed out 2 crew members doing exactly that. Russel stated they are required by their contract and safety policy to have swampers with each piece of equipment working onsite at all times for safety purposes. I told him that needs to change immediately. He told me it's not going to change and Bennett crew's would pull of the job site if needed. He said the company would be happy to talk to Hartman about this issue but nothing is going to change. He says once his parts arrive on Saturday and next Monday all crew members will be very busy throughout each work day. I told him I would pass this information on up the ladder. Bennett completed the excavation, install and backfill of 18\" pipe going from post screw pit to \ufb02ush pit. Then all pipe layers and helpers started welding pipe together for installation tomorrow between octagon pits and fiber barn along with 24\" pipe going from east octagon to \ufb02ush pit. They had 2 large 323 excavators working and 306 mini excavator with skid steer working along side all of them.\nDVO delivered load of acid racks as well. Iron Horse completed dowels on north wall of fiber barn today but had to reschedule concrete pour for either Friday or Monday due to the wrong size anchor bolts. I asked Russel if he was going to start digging more footings for the fiber barn like he told David Jenkins. He said \"no Bennett does not do concrete work \".... He told me that Hayden completely understands there process of working. See time cards from yesterday and today.","subs":[],"survey":[{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""}],"sig":"raken/sig/2025-01-16.png","sigTs":1737087060000,"source":"Raken PDF"},{"id":"raken-bluesky-2025-01-17","pid":"raken-bluesky","date":"2025-01-17","by":"Jeff Pool","site":[],"att":[{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-17-00.jpg","ts":1737135420000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-17-01.jpg","ts":1737135480000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-17-02.jpg","ts":1737135600000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-17-03.jpg","ts":1737135600000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-17-04.jpg","ts":1737149700000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-17-05.jpg","ts":1737149700000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-17-06.jpg","ts":1737152400000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-17-07.jpg","ts":1737152400000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-17-08.jpg","ts":1737152460000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-17-09.jpg","ts":1737152460000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-17-10.jpg","ts":1737152520000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-17-11.jpg","ts":1737152820000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-17-12.jpg","ts":1737153060000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-17-13.jpg","ts":1737155880000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-17-14.jpg","ts":1737155880000,"cap":""},{"url":"raken/photos/2025-01-17-15.jpg","ts":1737156000000,"cap":""}],"wx":[{"t":32,"c":"Clear","w":"14","p":".0","h":"69"},{"t":45,"c":"Clear","w":"8","p":".0","h":"51"},{"t":45,"c":"Clear","w":"26","p":".0","h":"58"}],"notes":"Iron Horse had a crew of 6. They completed the wall rebar on the north grade beam. Poured concrete footing on same grade beam starting at 2:00 PM.\nBennett had a crew of 11. They excavated for the underground piping on the south side of the fiber building.\nThey covered with sand and backfilled around the 18\" over\ufb02ow pipe between the post screw pit and \ufb02ush pit #2. Installed the 24\" over\ufb02ow pipe between mixing pit west and \ufb02ush pit #2.\nHad plans to trench for screw press underground piping but concrete trucks using fiber barn area as the path for a road to pour concrete in Barn 3. Quality Dairy set anchor bolts in concrete as Iron Horse was pouring footing.\nBennett set up safety fencing to prevent accidental fall into trench but wind blew it down. (See photo)","subs":[],"survey":[{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":