pe line from post screw pit to lagoon and then excavated 300' of trench and installed pipe to first clean out location. All 5 clean outs are welded with \ufb02anges. Bennett will continue excavation and pipe install tomorrow along with backfilling octagon pit so crane can set up Monday morning to start installation of pumps/agitators in octagons. Quality Dairy installed all anchor bolts and assembly's at south fiber wall footing. Iron Horse crew of 8 completed dowels at both footings of fiber barn.\nConcrete pour is scheduled for 9:30am Saturday. Quality Dairy cleaning out \ufb02ush/screen pits of mud and muddy water they dumped into them yesterday. We had lite rain last night onsite that required more mud removal for work areas access. Iron Horse worked 9.0 hours. Bennett worked 10.0 hours.","subs":[],"survey":[{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""},{"a":"N/A","d":""}],"sig":"raken/sig/2025-01-31.png","sigTs":1738380540000,"source":"Raken PDF"}]}